        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): suppress stdout/stderr stream errors in sandbox subprocesses",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where stdout/stderr pipe errors from Codex sandbox subprocesses could surface as unhandled Node stream errors, crashing the exec-server WebSocket bridge.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWhen a Codex sandbox process exits or its pipes are broken (e.g. the sandbox container is destroyed mid-flight), the Node stream layer emits `error` events on the child's stdout/stderr Readable streams. Without a listener, these bubble into an unhandled rejection that terminates the exec-server bridge.\n\nThe fix mirrors the same pattern used in `src/agents/sessions/exec.ts` and other sibling spawn paths: attach a no-op error listener to suppress the events while letting the process `close` handler remain authoritative.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCodex sandbox exec-server no longer crashes when a subprocess pipe breaks. Output collection and close signalling continue to work normally.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- The fix is a 3-line addition following the established `ignoreOutputStreamError` pattern used across `src/agents/`, `src/infra/`, and `src/auto-reply/`.\n- `process.on(\"error\", ...)` already covers spawn failures; the new listeners cover independent stream-level pipe failures.\n- No existing tests mock `child_process` in this extension; the runtime behavior is exercised by existing sandbox integration tests.\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex",
        "branch": "sunlit/fix/codex-processes-stream-errors",
